WAL — Time & Size, straight from the docs
Size
Each WAL segment file = 128MB
Prometheus always keeps a minimum of 3 WAL segment files
So minimum WAL footprint ≈ 3 × 128MB = 384MB (before compression)


Time
The guarantee is: at least 2 hours of raw data must be recoverable from WAL at any time (this matches the 2h head-block cycle — WAL must cover whatever hasn't been flushed to a block yet)
On a low-traffic server: 3 segment files might already hold well over 2 hours of data (fewer samples = segments fill slower)
On a high-traffic server: 3 segments (384MB) might not be enough to hold 2 hours of data (segments fill faster with more samples) → Prometheus will automatically keep more than 3 files to guarantee that 2-hour minimum is met
